{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558205-beast-feedback-please-increase-age-multiplier","id":558205,"title":"Beast Feedback: please increase age multiplier","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-17T07:05:06-07:00","id":558205,"title":"Beast Feedback: please increase age multiplier","content":"Beast with lairs above 5 add 20 years for each dot.<br /> <br /> This seems fairly short of a lifespan, not very long. The average person lives to be 70 something in the US IIRC, I presume most beasts don't make it to 5 dots. So most beasts only live to be 70 if they die of old age. But let's presume they make it to 5 and not 10, 7 dots will only put them to 110 which is not out of the realm of current human possibility. Moving on farther let's say you meet the beast at 20, and then again at 60, they will appear to be ~40 pretty good looking for a 60 year old, but they still will have obviously aged, thus no presumption of immortality, guess they got good botox. <br /> <br /> my suggestion, 50 years for each dot, no limitation on above above 5. Since you only get 10 dots your best case is the ripe old age of 600 (presumed max age of human about 100). They would seem immortal to people but still die of old age eventually","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T08:02:05-07:00","id":558255,"title":"","content":"Honestly, age doesn't matter in games beyond as a plot hook. From a game perspective, the age thing doesn't matter. It just doesn't affect play, so making Beasts live to a thousand years old as a house rule won't affect the game in the slightest. <br /> <br /> What a limited life span can do, however? It can become Aspirations, ambitions, drives, and the like. If you want immortality, aim for the Inheritance. <br /> <br /> Game design wants to include more plot hooks, not less. And I'm not sold on making Beasts longer lived naturally is going to add more story or drive to the game to make it more fun in any way. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T08:38:52-07:00","id":558299,"title":"","content":"The only thing that makes me blink is why the lifespan extension only starts at Lair 5. I don't see a lot of sense in that restriction, and I think it adds a bit of oomph to the average Beast if the &quot;each dot of Lair adds 20 years to your lifespan&quot; thing starts at 1.<br /> <br /> Mind you, it's not like Beasts <i>need</i> more 'oomph', but it feels right, y'know? Extends the bar on some older and more experienced Begotten comfortably reaching past 200 years old, without being so exceptional that they're among those that have achieved the Apex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-17-2015, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T08:44:59-07:00","id":558304,"title":"","content":"I'd probably tack on a &quot;you don't age in your lair either&quot; clause, a la Archmasters. That way you can have truly ancient hermit beasts that only show up outside every once in a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T17:05:08-07:00","id":558869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558205-beast-feedback-please-increase-age-multiplier?p=558255#post558255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, age doesn't matter in games beyond as a plot hook. From a game perspective, the age thing doesn't matter. It just doesn't affect play, so making Beasts live to a thousand years old as a house rule won't affect the game in the slightest.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does affect NPCs and &quot;era hopping&quot; games. Also the RAW doesn't really match the &quot;beasts assumed to be immortal but just live a really long time&quot; seems to me most of them only live slightly longer than humans.<br /> <br /> I'm not looking for immortality but I would like to see beasts live long enough to to seem immortal. I don't expect most beasts to live to old age anyways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":4046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","user":"xenoterracide","date":". 06-17-2015, 08:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T17:14:05-07:00","id":558875,"title":"","content":"Why should Beasts be long-lived? The inheritor forms, sure, but why just a Beast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T19:26:45-07:00","id":558979,"title":"","content":"because that's what the text thus far seems to say.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Beasts are immortal: False. While a Beast with a well-established Lair can live for a very<br /> long time, they eventually perish of old age. That assumes no Hero or other hazard gets them<br /> first.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T19:29:26-07:00","id":558980,"title":"","content":"A hundred extra years is a long time. That would put you alive through both World Wars and possibly back to the Taiping Rebellion while still letting you see the rise of the Internet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-17-2015, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T21:25:04-07:00","id":559039,"title":"","content":"and we circle to part of my original point most beasts wouldn't make it to lair 10, also being alive through both world wars and seeing the rise of the internet has been accomplished by humans, so you help make my point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-17T21:41:31-07:00","id":559045,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oldest_people\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oldest_people</a> <span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The longest undisputed lifespan for a male is that of </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jiroemon_Kimura\" target=\"_blank\">Jiroemon Kimura</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> of </span></span></span><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japan\" target=\"_blank\">Japan</a><span style=\"color:#252525\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> (1897\u20132013), who died in June 2013 at age 116. not easy as a human but since reach that as a human is hard even beasts getting that extra 40 years probably would only make it this far, in WoD this individual may have been a Beast according to the RAW currently, how else would you survive that long. And that extra 40 years? you aren't gonna be a young whipper snapper for most of it.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T02:52:25-07:00","id":559177,"title":"","content":"Before the revision, I always saw the lack of immortality as a sign of them having a foot in each world-human and monstrous.<br /> <br /> Anyway, why make long life a basic part of the template? A lot of monsters didn't live long enough to indicate immortality.<br /> <br /> Make an atavism, throw in something against drugs, poisons, and disease, title it &quot;Wickedness Never Dies&quot; or something like that.<br /> <br /> Or make it a greater lair trait &quot;Aged- Time and entropy claim all things, in your lair that is especially true. Food rots, eyesight dims, ears become less sensitive, bones become brittle and muscles weaker, etc, etc.&quot; And since beasts are immune to the traits of their lairs even if its not from their lair, such a beast would therefore not grow old.<br /> <br /> Or you know, both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 06-18-2015, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T03:10:55-07:00","id":559202,"title":"","content":"...Unless I missed something, Inheritance doesn't effect the Begotten's lifespan. In fact there is nothing to suggest the Merged or the Apex have anything than other the normal Beast lifespan. The Unfettered gets a pass as an Ephemeral Being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T03:23:14-07:00","id":559205,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's not actually in there. <br /> <br /> I mean, I immediately resolved to houserule it that way if it ever came up, but there's nothing in the text one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T05:05:43-07:00","id":559238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xenoterracide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558205-beast-feedback-please-increase-age-multiplier?p=559039#post559039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and we circle to part of my original point most beasts wouldn't make it to lair 10, also being alive through both world wars and seeing the rise of the internet has been accomplished by humans, so you help make my point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except I also included the 1850 Taiping Rebellion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558205-beast-feedback-please-increase-age-multiplier?p=559202#post559202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Unless I missed something, Inheritance doesn't effect the Begotten's lifespan. In fact there is nothing to suggest the Merged or the Apex have anything than other the normal Beast lifespan. The Unfettered gets a pass as an Ephemeral Being.</div> </div> </div> </div>You didn't miss anything, but the whole thread is about someone trying to get the rules regarding age changed. While I disagree about the Beast standard, I do think the Inheritances should be granted immortality. Apex is a goalpost. If a Beast doesn't want to accept their mortality, it's an even more enticing one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T05:56:58-07:00","id":559287,"title":"","content":"A dragon should be able to spend a few centuries watching over its hoard. Legendary monsters aren't supposed to die from old age, or suffer its outrages. I'd just double a Beast lifespan for every Lair dot after the 5th. That way we could have a few really old and powerful monsters hanging around, real living Legends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T06:10:14-07:00","id":559292,"title":"","content":"Now that seems a bit excessive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T06:13:51-07:00","id":559297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558205-beast-feedback-please-increase-age-multiplier?p=559287#post559287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A dragon should be able to spend a few centuries watching over its hoard. Legendary monsters aren't supposed to die from old age, or suffer its outrages. I'd just double a Beast lifespan for every Lair dot after the 5th. That way we could have a few really old and powerful monsters hanging around, real living Legends.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, Beasts aren't dragons, or legendary monsters. That's what the Apex inheritor is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T06:31:34-07:00","id":559302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558205-beast-feedback-please-increase-age-multiplier?p=559297#post559297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is, Beasts aren't dragons, or legendary monsters. That's what the Apex inheritor is.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I didn't talk about making them unaging outright. Frankly, making Beasts able to live longer is only interesting because of the stories you can tell it's unlikely to affect gameplay. And meeting storywise a longer lifespan means more options for NPCs; old Beasts could be from Antiquity or the Middle Ages as well as from the Victorian Era.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T07:10:43-07:00","id":559343,"title":"","content":"Well, if we want this huge age, specifically for those few Beasts of ultimate ages, then why not have a merit? Or an Atavism?<br /> <br /> Forever the Protector of the Hoard (*)<br /> Prerequisites: Beast, Lair 5+, Collector<br /> Your character is one of the few truly old Beasts. If no Hero comes to claim his life, he will be able to protect his Hoard forever. <br /> Effect: The character ceases to age.<br /> <br /> Ageless Monster (***)<br /> Prerequisites: Beast<br /> Your character does not age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T07:37:52-07:00","id":559362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558205-beast-feedback-please-increase-age-multiplier?p=559343#post559343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, if we want this huge age, specifically for those few Beasts of ultimate ages, then why not have a merit? Or an Atavism?<br /> <br /> Forever the Protector of the Hoard (*)<br /> Prerequisites: Beast, Lair 5+, Collector<br /> Your character is one of the few truly old Beasts. If no Hero comes to claim his life, he will be able to protect his Hoard forever.<br /> Effect: The character ceases to age.<br /> <br /> Ageless Monster (***)<br /> Prerequisites: Beast<br /> Your character does not age.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? Only the possibility really matters, not the means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T10:26:58-07:00","id":559526,"title":"","content":"Longevity (* - *****)<br /> Each dot of longevity raises your effective lair by your lair dots for the purposes of determining lifespan. This can raise effective lair over 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 06-18-2015, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T10:40:32-07:00","id":559539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558205-beast-feedback-please-increase-age-multiplier?p=559526#post559526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Longevity (* - *****)<br /> Each dot of longevity raises your effective lair by your lair dots for the purposes of determining lifespan. This can raise effective lair over 10.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is too... mechanic-y imo. <br /> <br /> I'd say that a better version would be <br /> <br /> Longevity (* - *****)<br /> Each dot of Longevity raises your lifespan by 20 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T12:56:09-07:00","id":559717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558205-beast-feedback-please-increase-age-multiplier?p=559526#post559526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Longevity (* - *****)<br /> Each dot of longevity raises your effective lair by your lair dots for the purposes of determining lifespan. This can raise effective lair over 10.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't it have been easier to say multiply longevity by lair to get effective lair?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T13:07:37-07:00","id":559736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558205-beast-feedback-please-increase-age-multiplier?p=559717#post559717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't it have been easier to say multiply longevity by lair to get effective lair?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lair by Longevity + 1, rather.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T15:52:09-07:00","id":559918,"title":"","content":"I don't want immortal beasts, just beasts that humanity would assume are immortal due to very slow aging","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T16:00:09-07:00","id":559925,"title":"","content":"How about a Vampire or Tremere lich inspired Nightmare able to feed from people's life force to extend the Beast's own life span?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-18T16:53:07-07:00","id":559968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558205-beast-feedback-please-increase-age-multiplier?p=559736#post559736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lair by Longevity + 1, rather.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, I forgot the adding to Lair part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T03:00:05-07:00","id":560580,"title":"","content":"Let's not forget that adding age as a merit... well sucks. From a PC standpoint, there's very little stories where such a thing matters at all, that's precisely why I made their lifespan infinite. Because it doesn't matter. Almost no PC would be buying it even for 1 experience point <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T03:54:04-07:00","id":560610,"title":"","content":"Yes you're right, which is why I'd package it with other benefits- a lair trait, or an atavism that protects against poison and disease as well, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T04:34:55-07:00","id":560625,"title":"","content":"Well, I'm looking at this thing from the standpoint of: It seems that people want such ages, to have that rare super old Beast, as a reclusive/plot point/etc. I don't see a reason to complicate it with packaging it up with other things. NPCs can have it... PCs can have it if they want to have their background stretch ages. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-20T21:27:31-07:00","id":562611,"title":"","content":"How many of those people are actually willing to pay points for this, which means their super duper old beasts is less powerful than a 15 year old? <br /> <br /> And if you give them something for nothing, then you ignore the fact that there's no reason to believe the majority of monsters from myth and legend are immortal- some specifically aren't unaging, others just don't live out past a human lifespan thanks to getting murdered by some Hero. <br /> <br /> For that matter, the immortal part of the beast is the soul- The minotaur is dead, long live the minotaur. Flesh dies, the legend lives on forever. A more appropriate form of immortality would be for the beast to remember their past lives like the serial reincarnate from Immortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T06:53:57-07:00","id":562963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558205-beast-feedback-please-increase-age-multiplier?p=559238#post559238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You didn't miss anything, but the whole thread is about someone trying to get the rules regarding age changed. While I disagree about the Beast standard, I do think the Inheritances should be granted immortality. Apex is a goalpost. If a Beast doesn't want to accept their mortality, it's an even more enticing one.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, that's an excellent point, and for some reason I entirely didn't think of it when I wrote the Inheritances. I've brought that up to Matt, so we'll see where it goes. My initial (<i>and entirely unofficial until/unless it sees print</i>) thought is that, for the Incarnates at least, it should be tied to their Myth. Perhaps as an innate thing, or maybe as something they can select. We'll see what, if anything, gets hashed out on that end.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T14:14:56-07:00","id":563398,"title":"","content":"Immortality upon Inheritance might feel like a gold watch after 30 years. I would suggest having aging slowed to a crawl upon Inheritance, so as long as the Myth is remembered, a Beast could live for thousands of years. It would keep the Beasts active and leaves all options open. They would still be effectively immortal. No mechanics would really be necessary. They could be thousands of years old <i>and</i> not long for this world. Anything more than a thousand years and the significance of age is lost anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T05:01:33-07:00","id":564002,"title":"","content":"Speaking of Apex, does anyone else think that it's a problem that a Beast could theoretically accidentally reach Apex? I feel like it should take a little bit more effort than spending some exp and pushing a Hero around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T05:23:12-07:00","id":564017,"title":"","content":"Because earning 175 beats is a piece of cake, obviously...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T06:42:33-07:00","id":564058,"title":"","content":"35 XP, Big deal... Been in a werewolf game that has the equivalent of over 100 XP in the new system (close on 600 Beats equivalent, and that with incrementing costs rather than static). 35 XP is chump change.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And to point out, none of the characters had anywhere near a Primal Urge of 8. The closest was the Itheaur with PU 5, and the Cahalith with PU 4.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 06-22-2015, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T06:49:21-07:00","id":564075,"title":"","content":"Narratively speaking Lair 8 seems extremely significant, even if you think 35 XP is not a big deal (and it <i>is</i> supposed to be, it's what a Mover And Shaker vampire has according to the xp count in Requiem 2e, or a Champion Of Hell demon according to the Descent corebook).<br /> <br /> And considering how you have to control the entire confrontation with the Hero and take charge of the story to form a Myth, I wouldn't say it can happen accidentally, even if you fulfill the Lair 8 requirement and don't take lethal or aggravated damage when confronting a Hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-22-2015, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T07:02:03-07:00","id":564092,"title":"","content":"I don't think a beast could take on a hunter with as much ease as required if they <i>only</i> spent xp on Lair anyway (seriously who would even do that?) so we're probably talking a much higher total. Probably closer to the aforementioned werewolf game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T07:12:48-07:00","id":564100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558205-beast-feedback-please-increase-age-multiplier?p=564075#post564075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Narratively speaking Lair 8 seems extremely significant, even if you think 35 XP is not a big deal (and it <i>is</i> supposed to be, it's what a Mover And Shaker vampire has according to the xp count in Requiem 2e, or a Champion Of Hell demon according to the Descent corebook).<br /> <br /> And considering how you have to control the entire confrontation with the Hero and take charge of the story to form a Myth, I wouldn't say it can happen accidentally, even if you fulfill the Lair 8 requirement and don't take lethal or aggravated damage when confronting a Hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>The comparisons of XP to Power Level in the guidelines have always been way off, in my opinion, especially in 1st Edition... They are a bit better in 2nd Edition, but are still a bit off. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T08:38:42-07:00","id":564153,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the XP to power comparison are waaaay off.<br /> There are some purchases you can make to have lots of power, like going straight for Majesty 5 or something similar.<br /> But besides that? Anything less than 30 XP is just a fart in the wind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T09:30:53-07:00","id":564194,"title":"","content":"That sounds less like a problem with the named experiences benchmarks and more of a problem with Beats assignment.<br /> <br /> I don't think people get that a baseline, 0 XP World Of Darkness character is already in many ways a very competent and above-average individual. A single Experience is, in a narrative context, already a noticeable measure of personal advancement.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I like that. I like that PCs are, unless you make very thin-spread decisions at character creation, hardly among the most average of janes and joes*. But see, there's a dissonance when you take in the Experience gain that can't really be eliminated in any game of this nature, between the speed of character progression from a mechanical standpoint and that of a real world standpoint.<br /> <br /> That dissonance can sometimes make things strange. The greatest example I've experienced was in my group's Vampire The Requiem chronicle. We started with some additional XP because all of our characters were Ancillae. But that's exactly what they were. Ancillae. And since it was our first time using the GMC update rules (though we started with the classic rules and switched shortly into the game), we didn't really have much of an instinctive understanding of 'how many Beats is too many Beats'.<br /> <br /> And then at one point we looked back on our sheets, and whelp. We just accidentally elders.<br /> <br /> Far as I'm concerned, NWoD player characters are supposed to be exceptional individuals. But there's a certain awareness of <i>how exceptional</i> <i>that is</i>, that players and Storytellers alike need** to understand things like the significance of the mechanical requirements of the Incarnate Inheritance; an effort of comprehension necessary to put into context how impressive some achievements are supposed to be, and to digest and manage the group's advancement in a way that fits the world and the story.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">*Have you ever tried playing a game where you and your group stat yourselves as accurately as possible and completely disregard the experience progression system in alternative of &quot;when it makes sense&quot;? Yeah. The difference is really noticeable.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">**Of course, how each group treats the dissonance mentioned above and establishes the standard for advancement and the exceptional nature of the player characters is up to them. From what I know, rarely will two groups (or indeed even two people) agree on every instance when discussing the scale of individual aspects of the story or setting. But the books <i>do</i> somewhat define the weight things have in perspective, although in an open ended manne</span>r.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":".  Elaborating because I'm not trying to tell people how to play their games. 06-22-2015, 12:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T11:16:23-07:00","id":564334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558205-beast-feedback-please-increase-age-multiplier?p=564194#post564194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds less like a problem with the named experiences benchmarks and more of a problem with Beats assignment. I don't think people get that a baseline, 0 XP World Of Darkness character is already in many ways a very competent and above-average individual. A single Experience is, in a narrative context, already a noticeable measure of personal advancement.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely think it's a problem with the named experiences benchmark, but it's not really a big deal. It just creates some false expectations that most people discover on their own and ignore. 0 XP by itself is not a metric of how competent a character is, because that character might use their starting dots to hyper specialize in a way that most people never do. But I honestly think that if you build realistic people with the system you will come up short much more often than not.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558205-beast-feedback-please-increase-age-multiplier?p=564194#post564194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">*Have you ever tried playing a game where you and your group stat yourselves as accurately as possible and completely disregard the experience progression system in alternative of &quot;when it makes sense&quot;? Yeah. The difference is really noticeable.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Avatar games are a lot of fun, but the starting stats almost always come up short. It would take the previously mentioned 30 XP to stat myself accurately and I'm definitely not an Elder and have not even spent XP on supernatural powers. Most of my friends also cannot accurately stat themselves without additional XP except for 'Stoner Bob' who is an awesome guy to hang out with but was never really ambitious.<br /> <br /> These days we don't play with anything less than 10 XP, unless we're playing high school students or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T11:25:55-07:00","id":564352,"title":"","content":"I... honestly feel like the opposite of that. About Avatar games I mean. xD<br /> <br /> Mind you when I'm making a regular character who is supposed to have a certain age or life experience, I always think to myself &quot;I wish I had X more Experiences to also give them this I feel like they would have&quot;. But that's not me concerning myself with realism, that's me trying to exactly fill out my idealized image of the character that's strangely precise and detailed floating around in my head.*<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*It's also a little bit of my munchkin nature talking and saying 'oh god but this is useful too' and 'i think they might need this' and the like.</span><br /> <br /> And I know very few people who are genuinely that perfectly filled out in real life**. Granted, I don't know you or your group, so I can't really make that sort of call about your level of competency in the context of the nWoD rules. That'd be beyond rude. So I'll take your word for it, but I guess we'll have to agree to disagree when we talk about the overall way of things.<br /> <br /> **In our mortal avatar game we overall matched the template or exceeded it by like 5 XP, so in hindsight maybe it is too much to say a baseline character is exceptional, but I really don't have the experience of most nWoD PCs being anything but very skilled or notably competent people in their chosen areas.<br /> <br /> In addition, maybe the XP Benchmarks are a little fiddly in places, but I don't feel like it's very noticeable. In most of them, anyways.***<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">***Although in hindsight I've always felt Demons were comparatively underpowered in terms of their XP benchmarks and starting abilities.</span><br /> <br /> I suppose in general it's not a very useful debate because people are more than the mathmatical sum of their very rough measured abilities and inherent traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 06-22-2015, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T12:07:03-07:00","id":564412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558205-beast-feedback-please-increase-age-multiplier?p=564194#post564194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds less like a problem with the named experiences benchmarks and more of a problem with Beats assignment.<br /> <br /> I don't think people get that a baseline, 0 XP World Of Darkness character is already in many ways a very competent and above-average individual. A single Experience is, in a narrative context, already a noticeable measure of personal advancement.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I like that. I like that PCs are, unless you make very thin-spread decisions at character creation, hardly among the most average of janes and joes*. But see, there's a dissonance when you take in the Experience gain that can't really be eliminated in any game of this nature, between the speed of character progression from a mechanical standpoint and that of a real world standpoint.<br /> <br /> That dissonance can sometimes make things strange. The greatest example I've experienced was in my group's Vampire The Requiem chronicle. We started with some additional XP because all of our characters were Ancillae. But that's exactly what they were. Ancillae. And since it was our first time using the GMC update rules (though we started with the classic rules and switched shortly into the game), we didn't really have much of an instinctive understanding of 'how many Beats is too many Beats'.<br /> <br /> And then at one point we looked back on our sheets, and whelp. We just accidentally elders.<br /> <br /> Far as I'm concerned, NWoD player characters are supposed to be exceptional individuals. But there's a certain awareness of <i>how exceptional</i> <i>that is</i>, that players and Storytellers alike need** to understand things like the significance of the mechanical requirements of the Incarnate Inheritance; an effort of comprehension necessary to put into context how impressive some achievements are supposed to be, and to digest and manage the group's advancement in a way that fits the world and the story.</div> </div> </div> </div>I waffle a lot on the age issue in games. Right now my stance on it is houserule it to your groups particular tastes.<br /> <br /> \u200bAlso, YeOfLittleFaith, from what I'm hearing I apparently need to be in one of your groups games.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1705-okami","name":"Okami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1705_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T12:11:10-07:00","id":564419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558205-beast-feedback-please-increase-age-multiplier?p=564352#post564352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose in general it's not a very useful debate because people are more than the mathmatical sum of their very rough measured abilities and inherent traits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, not to mention there are two major issues that mess with the metrics:<br /> 1) 11/7/4 is not a very good representation of real people, since we tend to have many 1s and 2s.<br /> 2) XP purchases are not equal. Merits and Supernatural purchases tend to be considerably better than Attributes or Abilities.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-22T21:24:51-07:00","id":564981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/558205-beast-feedback-please-increase-age-multiplier?p=562611#post562611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> How many of those people are actually willing to pay points for this, which means their super duper old beasts is less powerful than a 15 year old?</div> </div> </div> </div> I think that's a bad idea and none of the other games do this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if you give them something for nothing, then you ignore the fact that there's no reason to believe the majority of monsters from myth and legend are immortal- some specifically aren't unaging, others just don't live out past a human lifespan thanks to getting murdered by some Hero.<br /> <br /> For that matter, the immortal part of the beast is the soul- The minotaur is dead, long live the minotaur. Flesh dies, the legend lives on forever. A more appropriate form of immortality would be for the beast to remember their past lives like the serial reincarnate from Immortals. </div> </div> </div>that might be an interesting, and could kind of cover why some people think they lived before.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.pinterest.com/xenoterracide/chrod-inspirations/\" target=\"_blank\">Graphic Inspirational Photos for Chronicles of Darkness on Pinterest</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://chroniclesofdarkness.slack.com\" target=\"_blank\">Chronicles of Darkness Slack</a> (PM Me with Email for an Invite, then invite your friends)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4046-xenoterracide","name":"xenoterracide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"563"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}